StatusLifecycle v1 is live - C#, .NET 8, compiles. (Domain/StatusLifecycle.cs)

Contract rules:

The 9 statuses live in enum Status (Domain/Status.cs) - never use strings, never invent a 10th.
Before changing a request/delivery status, every class does:
if (!_lifecycle.CanTransition(cur, next)) throw new InvalidOperationException(_lifecycle.ExplainRefusal(cur, next));
then set the status. No direct status writes without the check.
Birth states: new DeliveryRequest starts at Status.Requested; new Delivery (created on quote acceptance) starts at Status.Accepted.
Need a transition that's not in the table (e.g. Scheduled → Cancelled)? Message me - I own the table, nobody forks it.
Next up from me: DeliveryEvent, then Delivery + payment stack.
Build order:

Reuben - UI can read any object's Status property now for display.
Clarice - apply rule 2 inside DeliveryRequest.MarkQuoted() and accept/reject paths.
Maleesha - AllocationCoordinator applies rule 2 on Accepted → Scheduled.
Everyone - run dotnet build once today; screenshot your first successful build for the report.

